---
// ============================================================================
// AI SUMMARY METADATA
// ============================================================================
/*
AI Summary Metadata:
title: ArcUp — Open Plasma Research for Ecological Repair
summary: ArcUp is an open experimental research framework developing plasma-based systems for ecological regeneration, working transparently to make research accessible and actionable.
keywords: plasma technology, ecological repair, open science, regenerative systems, plasma activated water, soil restoration, community research, ethical innovation
ai_content_highlights:
  - Open research framework for plasma-based ecological regeneration technologies
  - Develops water purification and soil restoration systems using controlled electrical discharges
  - Guided by Repractice Ethical Framework emphasizing transparency, accessibility, and life-serving technology
  - Four-layer logic: Technology → Water → Organisms → Ecosystems
  - Transparent, multi-scale research process aligning engineering with ecological accountability
*/

// ============================================================================
// IMPORTS
// ============================================================================
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArcCanvas from "../components/ArcCanvas.astro";
import PageNavigation from "../components/PageNavigation.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SectionDivider from "../components/SectionDivider.astro";
import Card from "../components/Card.astro";
import LinkButton from "../components/LinkButton.astro";
import "../styles/global-v2.css";

import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
import { buildSEO } from '../utils/seo';
import { EXTERNAL_LINKS } from '../config/constants';

// ============================================================================
// SEO CONFIGURATION
// ============================================================================
const seo = buildSEO({
  title: "arc^",
  description: "ArcUp is an open experimental research framework for regenerative plasma technology. We share our methods, data, and designs openly—guided by the Repractice Ethical Framework.",
  path: "/",
  siteUrl: Astro.site,
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  bodyClass="page-home"
  seo={seo}
  navActive="home"
>
  <!-- PERFORMANCE: ArcCanvas loaded in before-header slot for optimal visual hierarchy -->
  <ArcCanvas slot="before-header" />

  <!-- SEMANTIC: Main landmark with proper labeling for screen readers -->
  <main id="main-content" class="page-shell" aria-labelledby="main-title">

    <!-- ========================================================================
         HERO SECTION
         Primary introduction communicating core mission and research framework
         ======================================================================== -->
    <header class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="main-title">
      <!-- ACCESSIBILITY: Eyebrow provides context before main heading -->
      <p class="eyebrow">Open Research for a Thriving Earth</p>

      <!-- SEMANTIC: h1 as primary page heading with hero-title class for large display -->
      <h1 id="main-title" class="hero-title">arc^</h1>

      <!-- Lead paragraph emphasizing key mission -->
      <p class="lead">
        <em>ArcUp</em> is an open experimental research framework advancing
        <strong>plasma-based systems for ecological repair.</strong>
      </p>

      <!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: content-prose for multi-paragraph text blocks -->

      <div class="content-prose">
        <p>
          Each experiment is a step toward a thriving Earth. We design and build
          plasma technologies as instruments for ecological functionality.
          Through them, we observe how controlled energy transforms water
          chemistry, influences biological processes, and supports the recovery
          of ecosystems. Each experiment links engineering with ecology.
        </p>
        <p>
          Workspace holds the technical detail—schematics, protocols, and
          walkthroughs—available once verification is complete. This keeps
          practice responsible while allowing anyone who wishes to learn to do
          so safely.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every project follows the
          <a
            href="https://repractice.xbyali.page"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >Repractice Ethical Framework</a
          >, which defines transparency, reproducibility, and accountability to
          the commons as baseline conditions for participation.
        </p>
      </div>


      <!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: section-cta for action buttons -->
      <div class="section-cta">
        <LinkButton
          href={withBase("/projects")}
          variant="primary"
          icon="arrow-right"
          >Explore Projects</LinkButton
        >
        <LinkButton
          href={withBase("/about")}
          variant="outline"
          icon="arrow-right"
          >About ArcUp</LinkButton
        >
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- VISUAL: Subtle divider for section rhythm -->
    <SectionDivider />

    <!-- ========================================================================
         RESEARCH FRAMEWORK SECTION
         Four-layer logic presented in accessible card grid
         ======================================================================== -->
    <section class="page-section page-section--center" aria-labelledby="research-framework-heading">
      <!-- COMPONENT: SectionHeader for consistent heading pattern -->
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Our Research Framework"
        title="From Energy to Ecosystems"
        subtitle="ArcUp studies how plasma interacts across four connected scales — from device to droplet, organisms to ecosystems."
        align="center"
      />

      <!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: card-grid--4 forces 4 columns on desktop -->
     <div class="card-grid card-grid--4" role="list">
        <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
          <h3>Technology</h3>
          <p>
            We develop and test plasma architectures that convert electrical
            energy into controlled discharge environments. Research spans
            community-built prototypes and institutional platforms, focusing on
            safety validation, reproducibility, and open-hardware standards.
          </p>
          <p class="card-note">
            <em
              >Focus: dielectric-barrier discharges, circuit optimization,
              modular design, and scalable applications.</em
            >
          </p>
        </Card>

        <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
          <h3>Water Systems</h3>
          <p>
            Water is the first interface between plasma energy and matter.
            Studies measure how reactive species alter chemical composition,
            oxidation–reduction balance, and contaminant breakdown, linking
            bench results to field applications.
          </p>
          <p class="card-note">
            <em
              >Focus: advanced oxidation mechanisms, desalination and water
              reuse, kinetics, pollutant and pathogen degradation.</em
            >
          </p>
        </Card>

        <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
          <h3>Organisms</h3>
          <p>
            We examine how plasma-treated environments influence microbial
            populations, plants, and higher organisms. Experiments link
            molecular data with physiological responses to evaluate benefit,
            risk, and repeatability across taxa.
          </p>
          <p class="card-note">
            <em
              >Focus: plant stress adaptation, microbiome communities, genetic
              and non-genetic responses, inheritance, and fitness.</em
            >
          </p>
        </Card>

        <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
          <h3>Ecosystems</h3>
          <p>
            At the largest scale, we test whether local plasma interventions can
            foster systemic resilience. Field and mesocosm studies integrate
            plasma processes into wetlands, soil–water interfaces, and
            regeneration designs to model long-term ecological repair.
          </p>
          <p class="card-note">
            <em
              >Focus: ecological functionality, systems theory, coupling and
              cycling dynamics, ecosystem processes and resilience, adaptive
              regeneration modelling.</em
            >
          </p>
        </Card>
      </div>

      <p class="content-prose text-center">
        Together, these scales form a continuum of repair—from energy generation
        to ecological resilience.
      </p>

      <p class="content-prose text-center">
        Detailed methods and safety information are available through Workspace
        once verification is complete, ensuring open learning remains safe and
        accountable.
      </p>
    </section>

      <!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: section-cta for follow-up action -->
      <div class="section-cta">
        <LinkButton 
          href={withBase("/how")} 
          variant="outline" 
          icon="arrow-right"
        >
          Our Methodology
        </LinkButton>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- VISUAL: Divider between major content sections -->
    <SectionDivider />

    <!-- ========================================================================
         GETTING INVOLVED SECTION
         Invitation for students, researchers, and community members
         ======================================================================== -->
    <section class="page-section page-section--center" aria-labelledby="getting-involved-heading">
      <!-- COMPONENT: SectionHeader establishes section context -->
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Participation"
        title="Getting Involved"
        subtitle="ArcUp is collaborative infrastructure for those building knowledge toward planetary repair and regeneration.ArcUp is in its early stages — you can help shape its direction from the ground up."
        align="center"
      />

      <!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: card-grid--3 for three audience pathways -->
<div class="card-grid card-grid--3" role="list">
  <!-- CARD: Student participation pathway -->
  <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
    <div class="card-icon">🎓</div>
    <h3>For Students</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Interested in aligning your studies with open research?</strong>
      You can. ArcUp projects are built to integrate with coursework — you’ll develop a supervised plan that advances plasma applications for ecological benefit, while contributing to a shared dataset for reproducible science.
    </p>
    <p class="card-note">
      <em>What you’ll need: a clear proposal, supervisor approval, and a commitment to open licensing and safe practice.</em>
    </p>
  </Card>

  <!-- CARD: Researcher collaboration pathway -->
  <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
    <div class="card-icon">🔬</div>
    <h3>For Researchers</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Seeking a field that values both rigor and openness?</strong>
      ArcUp’s early frameworks invite validation, replication, and co-development. Your expertise strengthens collective understanding of plasma–water systems and helps define responsible methods for applied ecological research.
    </p>
    <p class="card-note">
      <em>What’s available: emerging research questions, experimental frameworks, and opportunities for method refinement.</em>
    </p>
  </Card>

  <!-- CARD: General community participation pathway -->
  <Card as="article" variant="surface" hover={true} role="listitem">
    <div class="card-icon">🌍</div>
    <h3>For Practitioners & Collectives</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>Working independently or within a community lab?</strong>
      You can apply ArcUp technologies under shared safety and reporting standards. Projects remain locally governed but contribute results to a common research archive for ecological restoration.
    </p>
    <p class="card-note">
      <em>Getting started: review documentation in Workspace and connect with others exploring similar contexts.</em>
    </p>
  </Card>
</div>

<!-- UNIVERSAL PATTERN: section-cta for primary engagement actions -->
<div class="section-cta">
  <LinkButton 
    href={withBase("/join")} 
    variant="primary" 
    icon="arrow-right"
  >
    Join the Community
  </LinkButton>
  <LinkButton 
    href={EXTERNAL_LINKS.discord}
    variant="outline" 
    icon="external"
  >
    Explore Workspace
  </LinkButton>
</div>

<!-- SHARED COMMITMENTS: licensing, safety, commons -->
<div class="card-unifying-text">
  <h4>Openness · Safety · Shared Commons</h4>
  <p>
    ArcUp operates as open scientific infrastructure. All data, designs, and documentation are released under open licenses that protect freedom of use while preventing enclosure or harmful application. Knowledge flows openly, but always with responsibility.
  </p>
  <p>
    Safety is foundational. Every project follows electrical, chemical, and ecological standards, and any potential risk triggers review before continuation. Transparency exists to protect, not to pressure.
  </p>
  <p>
    Together these commitments form a living commons — where credit is shared, results remain accessible, and collaboration serves ecological repair. Joining ArcUp means contributing to knowledge that circulates, not extracts.
  </p>
</div>

    </section>

    <!-- VISUAL: Divider maintains rhythm before navigation -->
    <SectionDivider />

  </main>
</BaseLayout>